    <h2>What Is the Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>Unlike other treats that rely on unbaked dough chunks, the Choco Brownie Extreme is loaded with real, oven-baked chocolate brownies sliced into bite-sized morsels. These dense bakery pieces deliver a delightfully chewy mouthfeel that contrasts beautifully against silky vanilla soft serve and thick chocolate fudge syrup. It delivers a noticeably darker, more sophisticated chocolate profile than the sweeter, lighter <a href="/items/brownie-batter-blizzard">Brownie Batter Blizzard</a>.</p>
  <p>View all 2026 DQ prices and categories on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Who Should Order Choco Brownie Extreme</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order this if:</strong> You want maximum chocolate intensity in a Blizzard. If you are the person who always picks the darkest chocolate option on any dessert menu, this is your Blizzard.</li>
    <li><strong>Order <a href="/items/brownie-batter-blizzard">Brownie Batter</a> instead if:</strong> You want a sweeter, dessert-adjacent chocolate flavor rather than the intensity of baked brownie pieces.</li>
    <li><strong>Order <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo</a> instead if:</strong> You want a more moderate chocolate hit with cookie crunch rather than brownie depth.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>DQ Cake Connection</h2>
  <p>Die-hard chocolate fans can take this flavor home for birthdays and parties! Dairy Queen offers this recipe as a pre-ordered <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">DQ Blizzard Cake</a>, combining layers of real fudge brownie, chocolate crunch, and soft serve into a show-stopping ice cream cake that easily feeds eight to ten guests.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Choco Brownie Extreme</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>510</td><td>Darkest chocolate, baked pieces</td></tr><tr><td>Brownie Batter Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>530</td><td>Sweeter batter pieces, lighter</td></tr><tr><td>Cookie Dough Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>590</td><td>Sweet baked-good, not as dark</td></tr><tr><td>Royal Oreo® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>490</td><td>Cookie crunch + fudge center</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.99) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.79) at 510 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

